  "body": "**What's missing:** the GUI's mesh repair, `RepairModel` (`crates/app/src/commands/repair_model.rs`, M13.11), has no MCP tool. The `camcraft-mcp` skill lists it as remaining gap 3. An agent driving `camcraft-cli mcp` that imports an STL with an open edge or near-duplicate vertices can see the damage, but can't fix it headlessly. The only way is the Model page's Repair button (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs`, `CommandKind::RepairModel`).\n\n**Neighbour that works:** the GUI path queues `RepairModel { name, weld_tol, max_hole_edges }` (defaults 0.001 mm and 256 edges, `RepairUi::default`), and `crates/app/tests/repair_model.rs` pins it at the command level.\n\n**Done means:**\n- A `repair_model { name, weld_tol?, max_hole_edges? }` tool runs `RepairModel::new` through `env.history`, so it is one undo step that restores the exact previous facets. The defaults match the GUI's: 0.001 mm and 256 edges.\n- It returns the command's `RepairReport` as data: vertices and triangles before and after, `welded`, `dropped`, `holes_filled`, `triangles_added`, and the one-line `summary()`.\n- `RepairModel`'s refusals come back as tool errors, by name: an unknown name, setup furniture, a bad tolerance, a budget under 3 edges, a `geometry::repair` refusal, and \"nothing to repair\".\n- In-process JSON-RPC tests pin all three: an open-box STL gets its hole filled, undo and redo work, and the refusals enter no history.\n\nLabels per AGENTS.md for an agent-filed issue: `enhancement`, `P2`, `area:ui`, `source:agent` (this account can't set labels).\n",
